      "content": [],
      "prompt": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "A quadratic function $C$ models the coefficient of lift of a flying disc, where $x$ is the angle of\nincidence, in degrees, and $30 \\le x \\le 45$. The function estimates that the maximum value of the\ncoefficient of lift is 1.74, achieved when the angle of incidence is 41 degrees. Which equation\ncould define $C$?"
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "kind": "editable-pdf-source",
        "sourceSetId": "pdf-98ab9fd1c3274aa4b3669c900f2beb27",
        "sourceQuestionId": "m1-q3"
      },
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "choice-a",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$$C ( x )=- 0.005 ( x - 1.74 ) 2+41$$"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-b",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$$C ( x )=0.005 ( x+1.74 ) 2+41$$"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-c",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$$C ( x )=- 0.005 ( x - 41 ) 2+1.74$$"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-d",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$$C ( x )=0.005 ( x+41 ) 2+1.74$$"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
