      "content": [],
      "prompt": [
        {
          "type": "markdown",
          "text": "At the beginning of an experiment, the temperature of a liquid is 23 degrees Celsius (\n℃\n). During\nthe first 4.0 minutes of the experiment, the temperature of the liquid increases at an average rate\nof $7.5 C$\n$$\\circ$$\nper minute. Then, the temperature of the liquid increases at a constant\nrate of $2.6 C$\n$$\\circ$$\nper minute. If the temperature of the liquid reaches 61℃\n$x$ minutes after the beginning of the experiment, where $x \\gt 4.0$, which equation represents this\nsituation?"
        }
      ],
      "source": {
        "kind": "editable-pdf-source",
        "sourceSetId": "pdf-98ab9fd1c3274aa4b3669c900f2beb27",
        "sourceQuestionId": "m2-q3"
      },
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "choice-a",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$$61=2.6 x+23$$"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-b",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$$61=2.6 ( x - 4.0 )+30$$"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-c",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$$61=2.6 x+53$$"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "choice-d",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "markdown",
              "text": "$$61=2.6 ( x - 4.0 )+53$$"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
